  "id": "Compound::DB00144 - Gene::55512",
  "verbalization": "Phosphatidylserine interacts with Smpd4, which is involved in the catabolic and metabolic processes of sphingomyelin. These processes are linked to the function of Smpd3, suggesting a potential role for Phosphatidylserine in modulating Smpd3 activity. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Phosphatidylserine may influence Smpd3 through its interaction with Smpd4, which in turn affects sphingomyelin metabolism. The overlapping pathways highlight a shared role in lipid metabolism, suggesting that Phosphatidylserine could act as a regulator of Smpd3 through a mechanism involving Smpd4. The integration of these findings implies that Phosphatidylserine may contribute to the regulation of sphingomyelin-related processes, potentially through a mechanism that involves Smpd4 and Smpd3.",
